{"id":166,"name":"ledian","speciesId":166,"dex":166,"form":"normal","generation":2,"types":["bug","flying"],"stats":{"hp":55,"attack":35,"defense":50,"special-attack":55,"special-defense":110,"speed":85},"abilities":[{"name":"swarm","hidden":false},{"name":"early-bird","hidden":false},{"name":"iron-fist","hidden":true}],"height":14,"weight":356,"baseExp":137,"sprites":{"normal":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/other/official-artwork/166.png","shiny":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/other/official-artwork/shiny/166.png","icon":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/166.png"},"cry":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/cries/main/cries/pokemon/latest/166.ogg","genus":"Five Star Pokémon","flavor":[{"version":"gold","text":"When the stars flicker in the night sky, it flutters about, scattering a glowing powder."},{"version":"silver","text":"The star patterns on its back grow larger or smaller depending on the number of stars in the night sky."},{"version":"crystal","text":"In the daytime when it gets warm, it curls up inside a big leaf and drifts off into a deep slumber."},{"version":"ruby","text":"It is said that in lands with clean air, where the stars fill the sky, there live LEDIAN in countless numbers. There is a good reason for this - the POKéMON uses the light of the stars as its energy."},{"version":"emerald","text":"It is said that in lands with clean air, where the stars fill the sky, there live many LEDIAN. For good reason, they use the light of the stars as energy."},{"version":"diamond","text":"It uses starlight as energy. When more stars appear at night, the patterns on its back grow larger."},{"version":"soulsilver","text":"The spot patterns on its back grow larger or smaller depending on the number of stars in the night sky."},{"version":"omega-ruby","text":"It is said that in lands with clean air, where the stars fill the sky, there 